# AGENTS.md

Guidance for coding agents working in `{{ project_name }}`. `CLAUDE.md` imports this file.

## Project

{{ description }}. A typed Python {{ python_version }}+ script with one `main()` entry point and no runtime dependencies. `uv` is the only required tool: never use pip, virtualenv activation, or make.

## Commands

- Install or refresh the environment: `uv sync`
- Run the command: `uv run {{ project_name }} Ada`
- Test: `uv run pytest`
- Lint: `uv run ruff check .`
- Format: `uv run ruff format .` (check only: `uv run ruff format --check .`)
- Type-check: `uv run mypy {{ package_name }} tests`

## Layout

- `{{ package_name }}/core.py`: business logic, with no command-line or I/O concerns.
- `{{ package_name }}/cli.py`: the `main()` entry point; a thin layer that calls `core`.
- `tests/`: pytest suite, one module per source module.
- `pyproject.toml`: metadata, the console script, and all tool configuration.

## Conventions

- Type-annotate everything; mypy runs in strict mode and must stay clean.
- Use the standard library unless a dependency is clearly needed; add one with `uv add <package>`, never by editing `uv.lock`.
- Keep logic in `core.py` so it can be tested without running the command.

## Testing

- Add or update tests with every behavior change, including the failure path.
- Before reporting work as done, run the test, lint, format, and type-check commands above and report the real results.
- Tests must not use the network or real credentials.

## Safety

- Never read, print, or commit `.env` files, tokens, or other secrets.
- Do not change dependency version bounds without asking first.
- Prefer small, reviewable diffs.
